# IWR6843AOP mmWave Radar

The **IWR6843AOP** is a 60 GHz mmWave radar used in the Smart Firefighter Safety Vest for human and target detection.

## Purpose

The radar is mainly used to:

- Detect human presence
- Detect moving targets
- Detect stationary targets under the configured detection conditions
- Provide target information such as distance and movement data
- Support firefighter safety in low-visibility environments

## Working

The IWR6843AOP transmits millimeter-wave signals and receives the reflected signals from objects.

The radar processes these reflections and provides target information to the system. The radar data is then transferred to the processing unit through the configured communication interface.

The processed information can be displayed on the TFT display and used to generate safety alerts.

## Used In This Project

**Radar:** IWR6843AOP mmWave Radar  
**Frequency:** 60 GHz  
**Application:** Human/target detection  
**Processing:** Raspberry Pi 3 / VEGA-based system  
**Output:** Target detection information

## Role in the Safety Vest

The mmWave radar provides an additional sensing capability when visibility is poor due to smoke or darkness. It works together with the environmental sensors and other safety modules to provide useful information to the firefighter.

